{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FXCf2sm3thWokEvYCfoGLK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Skill Foundry â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-runnable)\n2\t\n3\tFull rationale + the single-repo constraint live in\n4\t`C:\\dev\\Skill-Foundry-Foreman-Plan-20260603.md`. This is the machine-runnable cut.\n5\t\n6\ttest-command: `python -m pytest tests/test_foundry_invariants.py -v`\n7\t\n8\tEach wave stages a Foundry-INTERNAL change and EXTENDS the invariant suite; the\n9\tgate above is the ground truth. Steps marked **FINALIZE (manual)** are cross-repo\n10\tand are NOT performed by Foreman (its repo-boundary guard would HALT on them) â€” do\n11\tthem by hand with copy -> verify -> commit -> sync -> drift-GREEN -> delete.\n12\t\n13\t**Convention for staging waves (load-bearing â€” read before staging anything):** a\n14\tskill/asset staged INTO the Foundry but not yet *delivered* to skills-master gets a\n15\t`map.json` entry with **`\"targets\": []`**. `bin/check-map-drift.py` treats an entry\n16\twith no targets as GREEN; adding a target path before the cross-repo delivery exists\n17\tmakes the drift check RED and fails the gate. Delivery (populating `targets`) is the\n18\tmanual FINALIZE step, never part of a Foreman wave. When you extend\n19\t`tests/test_foundry_invariants.py`, only ADD assertions (never weaken/remove existing\n20\tones) â€” anti-test-weakening will HALT a wave that drops a test without a citation.\n21\t\n22\t## Wave 1 â€” Stage Skills-and-Agent-Tips into the Foundry\n23\tDeliver: copy `C:\\dev\\Skills and Agent Tips` (and `C:\\dev\\Skills and Agent`) content\n24\tinto Foundry `notes/`; add a `map.json` entry naming it. Extend the suite: `notes/`\n25\tis populated and the drift check stays GREEN. Accept: `pytest -v` GREEN.\n26\tFINALIZE (manual, cross-repo): repoint ~8 external refs (incl. aurora README/CLAUDE/NOTES);\n27\tafter drift-GREEN, delete the loose source.\n28\t\n29\t## Wave 2 â€” Stage .critique-scratch (+ v1.1) into the Foundry (copy-only)\n30\tDeliver: copy both into Foundry `tools/critique-scratch/`; add a `map.json` entry;\n31\tmark **copy-only** (a live write target of `t2r-proxy.mjs` â€” source stays). Extend\n32\tthe suite: copies present and match a recorded content hash; drift GREEN.\n33\tAccept: `pytest -v` GREEN. (No source deletion â€” copy-only by design.)\n34\t\n35\t## Wave 3 â€” Reconcile Expert-Coder-Win11 reference\n36\tDeliver: record the canonical source (`skills-master/expert-coder`) in `map.json`;\n37\tstage only genuinely Foundry-authored notes. Extend the suite: the MAP names the\n38\tcanonical and no Foundry copy claims authorship over it. Accept: `pytest -v` GREEN.\n39\tFINALIZE (manual): triage the ~13 \"canonical\" refs; reconcile/delete the loose\n40\t`C:\\dev\\Expert-Coder-Win11`.\n41\t\n42\t## Wave 4 â€” Governance docs\n43\tDeliver: Foundry `docs/` with `SKILL-PRODUCTIONIZATION-CHECKLIST.md` (copied from\n44\tAgentic-Home), a seeded `CONTRIBUTING.md`, the staged `SKILL.template.md` (from\n45\t`C:\\dev\\Skill-Foundry-SKILL.template.md`), and a `map.json` pointer to the\n46\t`researchOne` gold-standard exemplar. Extend the suite: each governance file present\n47\tand non-empty; the template parses; the checklist contains its 5 gates.\n48\tAccept: `pytest -v` GREEN.\n49\t\n50\t## Wave 5 â€” Lock in the project-manager invariant\n51\tDeliver TWO things so the wave has a real in-repo deliverable (a pure test-only wave\n52\ttrips the vacuous-GREEN guard): (a) add a `project-manager` entry to `map.json` â€”\n53\t`\"canonical_external\": true`, `\"source\": \"C:\\\\dev\\\\Agentic-Home\\\\skills-master\\\\project-manager\"`,\n54\t`\"targets\": []`, with a `note` that skills-master is the canonical source (mirror the\n55\t`expert-coder` entry); and (b) an invariant test wrapping `skills-master/project-manager/bin`\n56\tpm-regressions (3/3) + a bin hash match, asserting `decompose.mjs` is the 113-line\n57\thardened version. The new `map.json` entry is the in-repo deliverable the invariant\n58\tsuite exercises. Accept: `pytest -v` GREEN (pm-regressions exit 0; drift stays GREEN).\n59\tFINALIZE (manual, cross-repo, outward): reconcile the 9 divergent SKILL.md bodies;\n60\tretire/untrack the kit from Agentic-Home; push canonical -> published repo (never a\n61\tForeman auto-push).\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a94821a-4842-40c4-8cf2-84032519ab23","uuid":"4b8f20c4-7a92-4f4e-9e6c-05cd5c3cfc58","timestamp":"2026-06-19T02:23:39.533Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/dev/Skill Foundry/IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md","content":"# Skill Foundry â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-runnable)\n\nFull rationale + the single-repo constraint live in\n`C:\\dev\\Skill-Foundry-Foreman-Plan-20260603.md`. This is the machine-runnable cut.\n\ntest-command: `python -m pytest tests/test_foundry_invariants.py -v`\n\nEach wave stages a Foundry-INTERNAL change and EXTENDS the invariant suite; the\ngate above is the ground truth. Steps marked **FINALIZE (manual)** are cross-repo\nand are NOT performed by Foreman (its repo-boundary guard would HALT on them) â€” do\nthem by hand with copy -> verify -> commit -> sync -> drift-GREEN -> delete.\n\n**Convention for staging waves (load-bearing â€” read before staging anything):** a\nskill/asset staged INTO the Foundry but not yet *delivered* to skills-master gets a\n`map.json` entry with **`\"targets\": []`**. `bin/check-map-drift.py` treats an entry\nwith no targets as GREEN; adding a target path before the cross-repo delivery exists\nmakes the drift check RED and fails the gate. Delivery (populating `targets`) is the\nmanual FINALIZE step, never part of a Foreman wave. When you extend\n`tests/test_foundry_invariants.py`, only ADD assertions (never weaken/remove existing\nones) â€” anti-test-weakening will HALT a wave that drops a test without a citation.\n\n## Wave 1 â€” Stage Skills-and-Agent-Tips into the Foundry\nDeliver: copy `C:\\dev\\Skills and Agent Tips` (and `C:\\dev\\Skills and Agent`) content\ninto Foundry `notes/`; add a `map.json` entry naming it. Extend the suite: `notes/`\nis populated and the drift check stays GREEN. Accept: `pytest -v` GREEN.\nFINALIZE (manual, cross-repo): repoint ~8 external refs (incl. aurora README/CLAUDE/NOTES);\nafter drift-GREEN, delete the loose source.\n\n## Wave 2 â€” Stage .critique-scratch (+ v1.1) into the Foundry (copy-only)\nDeliver: copy both into Foundry `tools/critique-scratch/`; add a `map.json` entry;\nmark **copy-only** (a live write target of `t2r-proxy.mjs` â€” source stays). Extend\nthe suite: copies present and match a recorded content hash; drift GREEN.\nAccept: `pytest -v` GREEN. (No source deletion â€” copy-only by design.)\n\n## Wave 3 â€” Reconcile Expert-Coder-Win11 reference\nDeliver: record the canonical source (`skills-master/expert-coder`) in `map.json`;\nstage only genuinely Foundry-authored notes. Extend the suite: the MAP names the\ncanonical and no Foundry copy claims authorship over it. Accept: `pytest -v` GREEN.\nFINALIZE (manual): triage the ~13 \"canonical\" refs; reconcile/delete the loose\n`C:\\dev\\Expert-Coder-Win11`.\n\n## Wave 4 â€” Governance docs\nDeliver: Foundry `docs/` with `SKILL-PRODUCTIONIZATION-CHECKLIST.md` (copied from\nAgentic-Home), a seeded `CONTRIBUTING.md`, the staged `SKILL.template.md` (from\n`C:\\dev\\Skill-Foundry-SKILL.template.md`), and a `map.json` pointer to the\n`researchOne` gold-standard exemplar. Extend the suite: each governance file present\nand non-empty; the template parses; the checklist contains its 5 gates.\nAccept: `pytest -v` GREEN.\n\n## Wave 5 â€” Lock in the project-manager invariant\nDeliver TWO things so the wave has a real in-repo deliverable (a pure test-only wave\ntrips the vacuous-GREEN guard): (a) add a `project-manager` entry to `map.json` â€”\n`\"canonical_external\": true`, `\"source\": \"C:\\\\dev\\\\Agentic-Home\\\\skills-master\\\\project-manager\"`,\n`\"targets\": []`, with a `note` that skills-master is the canonical source (mirror the\n`expert-coder` entry); and (b) an invariant test wrapping `skills-master/project-manager/bin`\npm-regressions (3/3) + a bin hash match, asserting `decompose.mjs` is the 113-line\nhardened version. The new `map.json` entry is the in-repo deliverable the invariant\nsuite exercises. Accept: `pytest -v` GREEN (pm-regressions exit 0; drift stays GREEN).\nFINALIZE (manual, cross-repo, outward): reconcile the 9 divergent SKILL.md bodies;\nretire/untrack the kit from Agentic-Home; push canonical -> published repo (never a\nForeman auto-push).\n","numLines":62,"startLine":1,"totalLines":62}}}
