{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01SF1s3xSea5TUUHh8x64RKJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Skill Foundry â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-runnable): Grounded Summary\n\n**Structure & ground truth**\n- The plan is the machine-runnable cut of a fuller rationale doc kept at `C:\\dev\\Skill-Foundry-Foreman-Plan-20260603.md`; the single-repo constraint is documented there.\n- The ground-truth gate for every wave is `python -m pytest tests/test_foundry_invariants.py -v` â€” each wave must leave it GREEN.\n- Each wave does two things: stages one Foundry-*internal* change, and *extends* (only adds to) the invariant suite. Anti-test-weakening will HALT a wave that drops/weakens an existing assertion without a citation.\n\n**Foreman boundary rules**\n- Steps marked **FINALIZE (manual)** are cross-repo and are explicitly NOT run by Foreman â€” its repo-boundary guard would HALT on them. They're done by hand via: copy â†’ verify â†’ commit â†’ sync â†’ drift-GREEN â†’ delete.\n- Staging convention (load-bearing): a skill/asset staged in but not yet *delivered* to skills-master gets a `map.json` entry with `\"targets\": []`. `bin/check-map-drift.py` treats empty targets as GREEN; populating a target path before the cross-repo delivery exists turns the drift check RED. Populating `targets` is always the manual FINALIZE step, never a Foreman wave.\n\n**The five waves**\n- **Wave 1 â€” Stage Skills-and-Agent-Tips:** copy `C:\\dev\\Skills and Agent Tips` (and `C:\\dev\\Skills and Agent`) into Foundry `notes/`; add a `map.json` entry; assert `notes/` is populated and drift stays GREEN. Manual finalize: repoint ~8 external refs (incl. aurora README/CLAUDE/NOTES), then delete the loose source after drift-GREEN.\n- **Wave 2 â€” Stage .critique-scratch (+ v1.1), copy-only:** copy both into `tools/critique-scratch/`; add a `map.json` entry; mark **copy-only** because it's a live write target of `t2r-proxy.mjs` (source stays). Assert copies present + match a recorded content hash; drift GREEN. No source deletion by design.\n- **Wave 3 â€” Reconcile Expert-Coder-Win11:** record `skills-master/expert-coder` as canonical in `map.json`; stage only genuinely Foundry-authored notes. Assert the MAP names the canonical and no Foundry copy claims authorship. Manual finalize: triage ~13 \"canonical\" refs and reconcile/delete loose `C:\\dev\\Expert-Coder-Win11`.\n- **Wave 4 â€” Governance docs:** create Foundry `docs/` with `SKILL-PRODUCTIONIZATION-CHECKLIST.md` (from Agentic-Home), a seeded `CONTRIBUTING.md`, the staged `SKILL.template.md` (from `C:\\dev\\Skill-Foundry-SKILL.template.md`), and a `map.json` pointer to the `researchOne` gold-standard exemplar. Assert each governance file present/non-empty, template parses, checklist contains its 5 gates.\n- **Wave 5 â€” Lock in the project-manager invariant:** deliver TWO things to avoid the vacuous-GREEN guard (a pure test-only wave trips it): (a) a `project-manager` `map.json` entry with `\"canonical_external\": true`, source `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\skills-master\\project-manager`, `\"targets\": []`, mirroring the `expert-coder` entry; and (b) an invariant test wrapping the `skills-master/project-manager/bin` pm-regressions (3/3) plus a bin hash match, asserting `decompose.mjs` is the 113-line hardened version. Accept: pm-regressions exit 0, drift GREEN. Manual finalize: reconcile 9 divergent SKILL.md bodies, retire/untrack the kit from Agentic-Home, push canonical â†’ published repo (never a Foreman auto-push).\n\n**Cross-cutting claims**\n- `map.json` is the central registry tying staged Foundry assets to canonical sources and delivery targets; `bin/check-map-drift.py` enforces its consistency.\n- The plan deliberately separates *staging into the Foundry* (Foreman-automatable, in-repo) from *delivery/outward push* (manual, cross-repo) at every wave.\n\nNote (git state): per the index, the build lane has run through this plan â€” recent commits show waves 4 and 5 landed GREEN and the trio/foreman entries were repointed since."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1921,"cache_read_input_tokens":31553,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1921},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a94821a-4842-40c4-8cf2-84032519ab23","uuid":"791ee93c-4f14-477a-bd5f-e6e2b6f71f7c","request_id":"req_011CcBpiDwVJCfQioxszf4m8"}
